From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 23:41:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] codec2: keep platform metadata owned by the library in tests

C2SampleComponent_test enables __C2_GENERATE_GLOBAL_VARS__ before including
the platform headers. This emits the platform _FIELD_LIST vectors in the
test executable as well as in libcodec2_vndk. Symbol interposition causes
both initializers and exit destructors to operate on the same vectors,
leading to a Scudo double-free abort even when the test filter runs no tests.

Include platform types before enabling metadata generation, keeping the
macro enabled for the sample enum and struct declared by the test itself.
This preserves normal library and process teardown.

Origin: Local ThinkSmart View port
Base-commit: 937eb9047ec2f88620f1f6a4d9e407f6c869d91a
Apply in filename order within this project.

---
diff --git a/media/codec2/tests/C2SampleComponent_test.cpp b/media/codec2/tests/C2SampleComponent_test.cpp
--- a/media/codec2/tests/C2SampleComponent_test.cpp
+++ b/media/codec2/tests/C2SampleComponent_test.cpp
@@ -19,7 +19,6 @@
 
 #include <gtest/gtest.h>
 
-#define __C2_GENERATE_GLOBAL_VARS__
 #include <C2Component.h>
 #include <C2Config.h>
 #include <C2Debug.h>
@@ -27,6 +26,9 @@
 
 #include <unordered_map>
 
+// Platform descriptors are owned by libcodec2_vndk, not this test executable.
+#define __C2_GENERATE_GLOBAL_VARS__
+
 class C2SampleComponentTest : public ::testing::Test {
 };
 
